Found the bug: showModal calls closeModal, which schedules `setTimeout(() => modal.innerHTML='', 220)` to clear, then immediately sets new HTML. That timeout from the previous modal wipes the new content 220ms later! This explains the pause dialog disappearing after substitution (showPause → showModal → closeModal schedules clear → sets new pause → 220ms later cleared).

Also affects any rapid modal transitions: settings changes call showSettings which re-renders, likely also blank after 220ms. This is a significant UI bug. In showModal, don't use closeModal with its timeout; clear immediately. Fix showModal: cancel pending timeout or clear directly before setting HTML.

Implement: track a `_modalCloseTimer`, in closeModal store timeout; in showModal, clearTimeout(this._modalCloseTimer) then set innerHTML immediately (or call closeModal without timeout). Simplest:

showModal(html, opts = {}) {
  clearTimeout(this._modalCloseTimer);
  this.els.modal.innerHTML = ...;
  ...
  this.modal = opts;
}

closeModal() {
  const bd = ...
  if (bd) {
    bd.classList.remove('in');
    clearTimeout(this._modalCloseTimer);
    this._modalCloseTimer = setTimeout(() => { this.els.modal.innerHTML = ''; }, 220);
  } else {
    this.els.modal.innerHTML = '';
  }
  this.modal = null;
}

Also initialize this._modalCloseTimer? Not necessary.

This is a great catch. Fix it.

